R <pre><code># These two forms apply the same conditions:
idata |&gt; filter(v_call == "TRBV2", Tissue == "Blood")

idata |&gt;
    filter(v_call == "TRBV2") |&gt;
    filter(Tissue == "Blood")
</code></pre> <p>Filtering recalculates repertoire summaries by default. Chaining filters can therefore produce different results when a later condition uses a recalculated value such as <code>imd_proportion</code>.</p>
